-        "analysis": "'Private Credit Panic - Why Investors Are Rushing For the Exits' is a news-explainer title: a named asset class (Private Credit), an emotional state (Panic), and a 'Why' promise with a crowd-flight image (Rushing For the Exits). Unlike most of this channel's titles it carries no dollar figure, no 'you' and no personal threshold; the viewer must already know what private credit is to feel addressed. Same-channel macro/news-warning titles cluster in low-to-mid TYPICAL: HR6wU9Hb6xk 'Wall Street Just Gave a Dire Warning (You're Not Ready)' 1.21959x TYPICAL, v7uG773-wAY 'The Beginning of the US Debt Collapse is Here' 1.11089x TYPICAL, QlPqXGV491Q 'WTF Is Happening To The Stock Market?!' 1.20385x TYPICAL, TIrIi752GSc 'The Bond Market Is Breaking - Here's What It Does to YOUR Mortgage!' 0.61547x TYPICAL, mErWx9GiVUc 'You're Not Ready For What's Coming' 0.77667x TYPICAL, 1W9dzLgpU4k 'What The Average Person Should Do Before The Market Crash' 0.54346x TYPICAL. Counterexamples: bv5qS6sR4Bs 'Are You Ready For What's Coming?' 4.79096x STRONG (vague threat title that broke out) and Dgp4_ehMo9k 'If You Don't Understand Bonds, You Don't Understand Money' 13.70542x STRONG, an evergreen explainer of a 'boring' fixed-income asset framed as a personal knowledge gap rather than as news. At 1.19071x this video sits in the same band as the other news-warning titles; the descriptive pattern is that asset-class news framing lands TYPICAL on this channel while personal-gap framing of a similar asset class has broken out once. Eight titles; not causal.",
-        "search_demand": "Moderate topical search interest is plausible given 2025-2026 trade and mainstream coverage of non-traded BDC redemption queues (see event block), but 'private credit panic' is a news phrase rather than an evergreen query. Historical query volume, Google Trends and traffic sources were not fetched.",
